symbol rulebook
lines 0 29
hash 4c31af493bbbbab7
note Lists the files the working copy changed against the parent revision (jj or git) and fails on any that is part of the rulebook. A whole guarded file or tree counts on any change; a Cargo.toml counts only when its guarded sections ([workspace*], [lints*], [*dependencies]) differ, since an agent may still bump a version or add a feature; vocabulary.txt counts only when its synonym lines differ, since an agent may add words but not decide which of two words is the canonical one. This is the back-stop for the pre-tool hook's guards, which a shell command can slip past. The message says to undo it and propose the change instead.

step 1hpban
order 9
parent zakvb7
author ai
file xtask/src/gate.rs
symbol architecture
lines 0 26
hash f4273ea9294f95ef
note Reads the workspace members from the root manifest and each member's [dependencies] keys, and reports every dependency that is not in arch.rs DEPENDENCIES for that package. The message names the file the graph lives in and that only the owner changes it, so the fix is to propose the edge, not to route around it. Layering is held by the compiler (a crate can only use what it depends on) and this check holds the dependency list itself.

